Virtual Functions
For virtual functions
 It is the type of object to which the pointer refers that determines which function is invoked
TriangleShape T(W, P, Red, 1);
RectangleShape R(W,P, Yellow, 3, 2);
CircleShape C(W, P, Yellow, 4);
Shape *A[3] = {&T, &R, &C};
for (int i = 0; i < 3; ++i) {
A[i]->Draw();
}
